## 3️⃣ Bundler (Vite / webpack / esbuild / Rollup) version

If you are using a modern bundler, the flow is the same, but you need two extra things:

1. **ESM import syntax** (no default export).  
2. **`setWorkerUrl()`** – required for bundled builds so the internal WebWorker can be located.

Below is a **Vite**-compatible example (the same pattern works for webpack, Rollup, etc., just adjust the worker import).

### `src/main.ts`

```ts
// 1️⃣ Imports ---------------------------------------------------------------
import { Map, setWorkerUrl } from 'maplibre-gl';
import 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css';
import { PMTiles } from 'pmtiles';

// Vite-specific worker URL import (the `?worker&url` query tells Vite to emit a worker file)
import workerUrl from 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl-worker.mjs?worker&url';

// 2️⃣ Tell MapLibre where the worker lives ----------------------------------
setWorkerUrl(workerUrl);

// 3️⃣ Register the pmtiles protocol -----------------------------------------
const pmtiles = new PMTiles('https://YOUR_DOMAIN/path/to/your-file.pmtiles');

// The `pmtiles` library ships a helper that can be used directly with the
// global fetch, but we need to wrap it so that MapLibre’s internal fetches
// go through the protocol handler.
self.fetch = new Proxy(self.fetch, {
  apply(target, thisArg, args) {
    const [input] = args;
    if (typeof input === 'string' && input.startsWith('pmtiles://')) {
      return pmtiles.fetch(input.replace('pmtiles://', ''));
    }
    return Reflect.apply(target, thisArg, args);
  }
});

// 4️⃣ Initialise the map ----------------------------------------------------
const map = new Map({
  container: 'map',               // <div id="map"></div> in index.html
  style: {
    version: 8,
    sources: {},
    layers: []
  },
  center: [0, 0],
  zoom: 2
});

map.on('style.load', () => {
  // 5️⃣ Add the vector source ------------------------------------------------
  map.addSource('my-pmtiles-source', {
    type: 'vector',
    url: 'pmtiles://'
  });

  // 6️⃣ Add the line layer ---------------------------------------------------
  map.addLayer({
    id: 'my-lines',
    type: 'line',
    source: 'my-pmtiles-source',
    'source-layer': 'roads',   // <-- change to your actual layer name
    paint: {
      'line-color': '#0066ff',
      'line-width': 3,
      'line-opacity': 0.9,
      'line-cap': 'round',
      'line-join': 'round',
      'line-outline-color': '#ffffff',
      'line-outline-width': 1
    }
  });
});
```

### `index.html`

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>PMTiles + MapLibre (Vite)</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/node_modules/maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css">
  <style>
    html, body, #map { margin:0; height:100%; width:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div id="map"></div>
  <script type="module" src="/src/main.ts"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

### What changed compared with the CDN version?

| Item | CDN version | Bundler version |
|------|-------------|-----------------|
| **Import** | `import * as maplibregl from '…/maplibre-gl.mjs'` | `import { Map, setWorkerUrl } from 'maplibre-gl'` |
| **Worker URL** | Auto-detected (no call needed) | `setWorkerUrl(workerUrl)` – one-time call before `new Map()` |
| **PMTiles import** | From a CDN (`https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/...`) | From the npm package (`import { PMTiles } from 'pmtiles'`) |
| **Build step** | None (pure HTML) | Vite/webpack/etc. bundles the code and emits the worker file |

If you are using **webpack 5+**, **Rspack**, **Rollup**, or **esbuild**, the same `setWorkerUrl()` call works; you just need to import the worker URL in a way that your bundler can emit a file. Typical patterns:

```js
// webpack / Rspack / Next.js (Turbopack)
import workerUrl from 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl-worker.mjs?url';
setWorkerUrl(workerUrl);
```

```js
// esbuild / Rollup
import workerUrl from 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl-worker.mjs?url';
setWorkerUrl(workerUrl);
```

(If you forget this call, the map will stay blank and the console will show a `Failed to load worker` error.)

