## 2️⃣ Bundler version (Vite, webpack, esbuild, …)

> **Important v6 notes**  
> * MapLibre v6 is **ESM-only** – there is no default export. Use a namespace import (`import * as maplibregl …`) or named imports (`import { Map, setWorkerUrl } …`).  
> * When you bundle, the worker that does tile-parsing cannot be auto-discovered, so you **must call `setWorkerUrl()` once** before creating the map (see the “Worker URL” section at the end of this answer).  

```bash
# From your project root
npm i maplibre-gl pmtiles
```

### `src/main.ts` (or `main.js`)

```ts
// 1️⃣ Import MapLibre (named or namespace) and the worker-URL helper
import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';
import { setWorkerUrl } from 'maplibre-gl';
import 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css';

// 2️⃣ Import the PMTiles helper
import { PMTiles } from 'pmtiles';

// 3️⃣ Tell the bundler how to load the worker file.
//    Vite (and most modern bundlers) support the "?worker&url" query.
//    Adjust the query for your bundler if needed.
import workerUrl from 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl-worker.mjs?worker&url';

// 4️⃣ Register the worker URL **once**, before any Map instance is created.
setWorkerUrl(workerUrl);

// 5️⃣ Register the pmtiles protocol (once per page)
const pmtiles = new PMTiles('/data/my-tiles.pmtiles'); // relative to your public folder
pmtiles.addProtocol();

// 6️⃣ Initialise the map
const map = new maplibregl.Map({
  container: 'map',          // <div id="map"></div> in your HTML
  style: {
    version: 8,
    sources: {},            // we’ll add the source later
    layers: []              // we’ll add the layer later
  },
  center: [0, 0],
  zoom: 2
});

// 7️⃣ Add the vector source and line layer once the style is loaded
map.on('load', () => {
  map.addSource('my-pmtiles-source', {
    type: 'vector',
    url: 'pmtiles://my-tiles.pmtiles'   // matches the protocol we registered
  });

  map.addLayer({
    id: 'my-lines',
    type: 'line',
    source: 'my-pmtiles-source',
    // 👉 Replace with the exact name of the layer inside the PMTiles file.
    //    You can discover it by opening the .pmtiles in TileServer-GL,
    //    tippecanoe, or by inspecting the network request for a tile
    //    and looking at the `layer` property in the vector-tile JSON.
    'source-layer': 'roads',
    paint: {
      'line-color': '#0066ff',
      'line-width': 3,
      'line-opacity': 0.9
    }
  });
});
```

### `index.html`

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>PMTiles + MapLibre (bundler)</title>
  <link href="/node_modules/maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet">
  <style>
    #map { position:absolute; inset:0; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div id="map"></div>
  <script type="module" src="/src/main.ts"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

