## 3️⃣ How to discover the **source-layer name** inside the PMTiles file

The PMTiles archive is just a container for a set of vector-tile layers.  
You need the exact name that the tileset uses (e.g. `"roads"`, `"water"`, `"building"`).  

* **Quick-look method** – Open the `.pmtiles` file in a viewer such as **[PMTiles Viewer](https://pmtiles.io/)** or **[TileServer-GL](https://tileserver.org/)**. The UI lists the layer names.  
* **Programmatic method** – Fetch a single tile and inspect its `layerNames` array:

```js
import { PMTiles } from 'pmtiles';
const pm = new PMTiles('/data/my-tiles.pmtiles');
await pm.getHeader();               // optional, just to ensure the file is readable
const tile = await pm.getTile(0, 0, 0); // z/x/y = 0/0/0 (any tile works)
const { layers } = await tile.decode(); // `decode()` returns a GeoJSON-like object
console.log(Object.keys(layers));   // prints e.g. ["roads","water"]
```

Use the printed name in the `'source-layer'` property of the layer definition.

---

## 4️⃣ Full-stack checklist (so you don’t get stuck)

| ✅ What you need | ✅ How to satisfy it |
|-----------------|----------------------|
| **MapLibre v6** (ESM) | `import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl'` (or named imports). |
| **PMTiles protocol** | `new PMTiles(url).addProtocol();` – do this **once** before any `map.addSource`. |
| **Worker URL** (bundlers only) | `import workerUrl from 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl-worker.mjs?worker&url'; setWorkerUrl(workerUrl);` |
| **Correct source-layer name** | Look it up in the PMTiles file (viewer or programmatic fetch). |
| **CSP / CSP-compatible script** (if you need CSP) | The CDN ESM build (`dist/maplibre-gl.mjs`) works with CSP because it’s a module; just add the appropriate `script-src` directive (`'self'` or the CDN origin). |
| **No default export** | Use `import * as maplibregl …` or `import { Map } …`. |
| **No CommonJS `require()`** | Convert any `require('maplibre-gl')` to an ESM import, or use dynamic `await import('maplibre-gl')` if you must stay in a CommonJS file. |
| **`styleimagemissing`** (if you need runtime icons) | Use `map.setMissingStyleImageResolver(...)` – the old `styleimagemissing` listener no longer resolves the request. |
| **`map.transform`** (if you were using it) | Replace with public getters (`map.getZoom()`, `map.getCenter()`, etc.). No direct matrix exposure outside custom layers. |
| **`MapDataEvent`** (if you typed it) | Replace with `MapSourceDataEvent | MapStyleDataEvent`. |

